2. Free use

Subject to this license, the Licensor grants You a non-exclusive, worldwide, revocable only as provided below, royalty-free permission to:

(a) view and study the AirDeck source code;
(b) copy, clone, and fork AirDeck;
(c) modify AirDeck for Your own use;
(d) operate AirDeck for Yourself or Your own organization;
(e) use AirDeck to operate a radio station, including a commercial radio station or other revenue-generating media operation;
(f) redistribute an unmodified or Modified Version without charging for access to AirDeck itself, provided all applicable conditions in this license are met; and
(g) submit modifications back to the official AirDeck project.

AirDeck's normal version is intended to remain available without a software usage fee under these terms. Nothing in this license requires a radio station to share advertising, sponsorship, donation, music, broadcasting, or other unrelated business revenue merely because the station uses AirDeck.

3. Attribution and notices

Any copy or Modified Version that You distribute or make available to third parties must retain this license and applicable copyright notices.

A reasonably prominent attribution must identify the original project substantially as follows:

"Based on AirDeck – originally created by Ricardo Ramon Reimer Wiebe / RicoReWi."

You may accurately describe Your software as based on or derived from AirDeck, but You must not imply that an unofficial fork, modification, service, or build is an official AirDeck release or endorsed by the Licensor.

4. Free self-hosting

You may self-host AirDeck without paying a license fee when it is used by You or Your organization for Your own operations, including operation of Your own radio station.

You may also provide AirDeck without charge to third parties under the redistribution conditions of this license.

5. Commercial hosted services, subscriptions, and resale

This license does NOT grant permission to monetize access to AirDeck itself through a Hosted AirDeck Service.

Before You charge third parties for access to AirDeck or a Modified Version as a hosted service, subscription, managed AirDeck platform, reseller service, white-label service, or materially similar commercial offering, You must obtain a separate written Commercial Hosting License from the Licensor.

The Commercial Hosting License may provide for a revenue share, recurring fee, minimum fee, individually negotiated terms, or another commercial arrangement.

No particular percentage or commercial price is granted or promised by this public license.

This restriction does not by itself prohibit charging for unrelated services or business activities merely because AirDeck is used internally as a tool. For example, operating a commercial radio station with AirDeck does not automatically create a revenue-share obligation.

6. Paid installation and professional services

Unless a separate agreement states otherwise, this license does not prohibit charging for genuine consulting, installation, migration, training, development, or support work where the customer is not being charged for access to a Hosted AirDeck Service.

A service provider may not use this section as a workaround to sell recurring access to AirDeck while describing the charge solely as support, maintenance, administration, or another service.

7. Modified and community versions

Modified Versions distributed outside the official AirDeck project must be clearly identifiable as unofficial or modified where a reasonable user could otherwise mistake them for an official release.

You are responsible for Your modifications, hosting, support, security, compliance, and representations to Your users.

